They exercise the real initializer, BDict verification, IsReady, selected file,
immutable-file preservation, writable corruption deletion and download target.
The existing DeleteCorruptedBDICT browser test uses an empty assets directory
so installing a valid packaged dictionary cannot mask its expected failure.
Chrome unit_tests declares the actual BDICT as Linux runtime data so isolated
test packages retain the fixture; no renderer test target is required.

Parent checks after applying and packaging:
